records.full_description:
“Heaven declared the mountain immovable. The cultivator placed one palm against it and asked whether Heaven intended to defend that opinion personally.”

Classification: Secret Brute Inheritance

Prerequisite: CL 17+, Court of the Moving Mountain, hidden mountain-moving scripture

Action Type: Action
Factory Combat Bucket: action
Factory Routing: combat_action_row

Range: Reach or 30 feet against a tethered target

Cost: Expend Martial Focus

Use Limit: Once per week

Choose one creature, unattended object, temporary Barrier, or ordinary structure section.

##### Creature

Make one Brutal Shove with Advantage.

On a success:

ignore ordinary size limits;

move the target up to 100 feet in one legal direction;

apply up to three Manhandle talents you know;

treat any collision as Hammer with +6d10 collision damage;

the target makes a Constitution saving throw.

Failed Save: Become Stunned until the end of your next turn.

Successful Save: Cannot take Reactions until the start of your next turn.

##### Object, Barrier, or Structure

Make a Strength check against a GM-set DC.

On a success, choose one:

tear open a major breach;

shift the object up to 30 feet;

collapse one ordinary section;

turn the object into rubble;

force open one sealed mundane passage.

The Hand That Repositioned Heaven does not automatically move or destroy:

artifacts;

Formation cores;

Domains;

Secret Inheritances;

Realm-defining structures.

Those may still be contested or meaningfully damaged according to the GM.

