records.full_description:
When you win a Disarm attempt, you may bind the target’s object to your weapon instead of causing the target to drop it.

You may also bind a hand, natural weapon, or comparable attacking limb as though it were a held object.

While the bind lasts:

the target has the Grappled condition;

the bound object or limb cannot be used to make attacks;

you must remain within the reach of the weapon or Unarmed Strike used to establish the bind;

you cannot use the weapon or limb maintaining the bind to make attacks;

the bind ends if you become Incapacitated, release it at any time with no Action required, or move beyond the permitted reach.

If an object is bound, the target may release that object at any time with no Action required, ending the bind. Otherwise, the target may use its Action to make a Strength (Athletics) or Dexterity (Acrobatics) check against your Cultivation Save DC, ending the bind on a success.

Bind Weapon is a special form of Grapple. It does not require a free hand unless the weapon or Unarmed Strike used to establish the bind requires one.

