When a creature is Restrained by Whirlpool Prison, affected by Drowning Pressure, or inside your Court of the Endless Tide, you may use an action and spend 4 CP to seal it in abyssal pressure.

The target makes a Constitution saving throw.

On a failed save, until the end of your next turn:

it is Restrained;

it cannot speak clearly;

it cannot regain Hit Points;

it has Disadvantage on Constitution saving throws to maintain Concentration;

if it attempts to teleport, fly, or move through a planar or spatial technique, it must first succeed on a Water check contested by your Cultivation Save DC.

On a successful save, it is Soaked and cannot take Reactions until the start of your next turn.

